    profiles: "No DNS servers yet."
    servers: "No DNS servers yet."
    routes: "No DNS routes yet."
    health: "No DNS health observations yet."
  generated: "Generated"
  routes:
    missing_profile: "Missing profile"
    strict: "Strict"
    fallback: "Fallback"
  help:
    title: "Help"
    markdown: |
      ### DNS Profiles

      Enter a DNS server IP to add it to the list. `Port` defaults to `53`.

      - Lookup priority follows the list from top to bottom
      - If the selected profile fails, RelayGate continues through the current list order
      - The final fallback is system DNS

      ### DNS Routes

      DNS routes make selected host patterns use a specific DNS server. This is useful when one DNS provider returns a policy warning page or an incorrect host for a site.

      - `Host Pattern` accepts `example.com` or `*.example.com`
      - Host patterns placed in DNS Routes use only the selected DNS server and do not fall back to other DNS servers
      - Delete a route to disable that rule

      ### Host Pattern

      `Host Pattern` accepts these forms:

      - `example.com`: exact match for one domain
      - `www.example.com`: exact match for one full host name
      - `*.example.com`: match all subdomains

