  title: "Site Mounts"
  sub: "Mount a remote site under a local URL path. RelayGate fetches the remote site through the normal pipeline and rewrites links back under the mount path."
  add: "Add Site Mount"
  list: "Site Mount List"
  mount_path: "Mount Path"
  mount_path_note: "Local path on the proxy listener. Example: `/site/`."
  target: "Target Base URL"
  target_note: "Remote site base URL. Example: `https://example.com`."
  upstream: "Upstream"
  upstream_note: "Optional. Choose an enabled upstream proxy for this mount."
  rewrite_links: "Rewrite links"
  rewrite_links_note: "Keep browser navigation and resource URLs under the local mount path."
  none: "No site mounts yet."
  missing_upstream: "Missing upstream"
  summary:
    mounts: "Site Mounts"
  help:
    markdown: |
      ### Site Mounts

      A site mount exposes a remote site under a local path such as `/site/`.

      ### Target URL

      Target Base URL must start with `http://` or `https://`.

      ### Upstream Proxy

      You can choose whether this mount uses a specific upstream proxy. Empty means the normal direct path.

      ### Rewrite links

      When enabled, RelayGate keeps later navigation and resource URLs under the local mount path where possible.

