    unsupported: "RelayGate currently does not provide this ability. The script may not work fully."
    error: "RelayGate cannot parse this script file enough to run it."
  support_label:
    supported: "Supported"
    partial: "Partially Supported"
    unsupported: "Unsupported"
    error: "Error"
  intro:
    title: "Feature Introduction"
    body: "User Script v1 indexes local files under `data/user/user_script/`, records enabled state and match metadata in `data/state/user_script.bin`, and injects matching scripts into mutable HTML document responses. It is compatible support, not full userscript-manager parity."
  help:
    markdown: |
      ### User Scripts

      User Scripts scan local `.user.js` files and inject matching scripts into mutable HTML documents.

      ### Support Status

      `Supported` means RelayGate can process it normally. `Partially Supported` means compatible behavior. `Unsupported` does not block enabling. `Error` means it cannot be operated.

      ### Apply Timing

      Enable, disable, and file changes apply to pages loaded afterward.


